            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 50 year old male with isolated left main coronary artery disease was surgically treated with saphenous vein patch angioplasty. Surgery results are reviewed by coronariography 2 months later and we comment its use as alternative technique in selected cases.</AbstractText>
